const RUBRIC = `THE VERIFIER RUBRIC (binding for every role; cite a section as R<n>).
R1 ADMISSION. A finding is admitted only when ALL hold: (a) REPRODUCIBLE at the sha under test, either from the running app (your own sidecar booted from that sha's binaries or source, the scratch jsdom harness, scripts/r15/vy.py) with the exact command and an output excerpt saved in its evidence file, or from the repo at that sha (path:line and the lines quoted); a claim about the world also carries the outside source's URL and a quote; (b) a PRODUCT defect: price drift inside the as-of skew, taste, a model's weak prose that the product does not render as data, and an upstream outage are not defects (an outage is kind environment, and only with a direct probe of the upstream saved beside it; a BSE or NSE 403 without that probe is not environment); (c) it survives the duplicate check R3; (d) its severity is set by R2 (the finder's is advisory).
R2 SEVERITY (docs/redesign/verification/r15/tooling/COMMON.md): critical = wrong money-relevant data shown as true, data loss, safety boundary; high = a core flow breaks or silently degrades, or a promise central to the product is missing; medium = a real defect or gap a demanding owner hits in normal use (or that bites the next maintainer); low = polish / edge. Do not pad: a finding that would not change a decision is not a finding. Every gate8 finding is critical.
R3 DUPLICATE CHECK against the register at the sha, BY ID AND BY REPRO: by id = the finding's register_id and every id or raw_id its evidence cites; by repro = the entries whose repro, title, files or root_cause name the same symbol, route, file or prompt shape AND the same mechanism. A match on a 'fixed' entry that reproduces again = a NEW entry whose note says 'regression of <id>' (the old entry is never reopened). A match on an entry that is open, blocked_tier4, needs_gui, removed_with_feature or not_a_defect = ATTACHED to that id (${EV}/ATTACHED.json {key, id, evidence_file}), not a new entry; except a not_a_defect whose rationale the new evidence contradicts, which is admitted as a new entry naming the contradiction. The same mechanism found twice in this pass = one item keeping every key. The DECISIONS_FOR_OPERATOR.md items still awaiting the operator (sections 3.x, 4.x and 5.1 to 5.10) are attached to their section, never filed as new.
R4 THE SIGNED-OFF CLASS (operator, 26 Sep 2026). 'The local model states a figure for a subject with no ok tool call behind it' is a known limitation: register entries ${SIGNED_OFF.join(', ')}; ${DEC} sections 4.9, 4.10, 4.11 and 4.12. An instance on the local model lane (Ollama, llama3.1:8b) is kind known_limitation, filed in ${EV}/KNOWN_LIMITATION_INSTANCES.json {key, class_entry, decisions_section, lane, prompt, evidence_file} against the matching entry. It is NEVER admitted as a new entry, never planned, never put through a fix round, and no writer touches the figure guard, agent_runtime._judge_clause or planner._NO_TOOL_CUE on its account. Outside the class, judged under R1: the same behaviour on a hosted lane (OpenRouter, OpenAI, DeepSeek); any product surface that renders a fabricated figure as data (a brief's structured metric card, a panel value, a tool result); a write that lands without the gate.
R5 NEEDS_GUI. A check that needs a real window, a native dialog (terms, keychain, save/download), a separate macOS user account's first launch, or pixel rendering without a proven browser seam is needs_gui: operator-attended, written to ${EV}/NEEDS_GUI.md with the exact manual steps and the expected result, and NEVER a fail, a pass or an admitted finding. The entries already needs_gui at the authoring head stay operator-attended: ${NEEDS_GUI_AT_AUTHORING.join(', ')}. The sheet lists every needs_gui item as DEFERRED; DEFERRED is allowed for needs_gui only and never rescues a FAIL.
R6 GATE 3 CLOSURE. Every admitted critical/high/medium entry, and every critical/high/medium register entry still 'open' at the sha, ends in exactly one of: (i) FIXED = a root-cause fix, pinned by a test in the repo's test locations that fails without the fix and passes with it, integrated with a green pnpm ci-local and smoke test at the head, and CERTIFIED in a fresh context (an agent that neither planned nor wrote the fix) from the running app with the original repro PLUS at least one fresh case of the same class the fix was not written against; or (ii) ADJUDICATED with a rationale a stranger can re-run: not_a_defect, not_reproducible at the head (the probe saved), environment (the direct probe saved), or blocked_tier4 (fixable only in a Tier-1 file or by reversing a locked decision, with its DECISIONS item drafted). 'Ran out of rounds', 'low impact' or 'model weakness' alone is never a rationale. Lows admitted by this pass are fixed or adjudicated the same way where writers have room, else listed with the reason. The register's pre-existing open lows are a counted backlog, not a gate item.
R7 THREE-FAILURES STOP. An entry's certification failures count across the whole R15 run: the failed certifications its register note records plus every not_certified verdict in this pass (a round verifier's or the re-proof's). At the THIRD failure the entry STOPS: it leaves the fix rounds and is never retried, its status becomes blocked_tier4, a DECISIONS item is drafted in ${EV}/DECISIONS_ADDITIONS.md (what was tried, the three failing verdicts with their paths, what fixing it would take), and the sheet lists it as stopped. A stopped entry counts as adjudicated for gate 3 only once that item is written.
R8 REGISTER STATUSES: only values the register already uses. Certified = fixed (closure_evidence '<head sha7> final-pass r<N>'); not_a_defect / not_reproducible / environment = not_a_defect with the verdict and rationale in note; Tier-4 or stopped = blocked_tier4 (tier4 true); needs_gui = needs_gui; anything else stays open with the reason in note.
R9 RUN-ENDING. ${RUN_ENDING_RULE}`

